;; classification.edn — HAND-AUTHORED. Fiat, and labelled as fiat.
;;
;; One entry per operator turn in the pinned window, keyed by the store's
;; evidence id. Two fields are judgement and two are lookups:
;;
;;   :kind      judgement — the turn kind, named in this excursion's own words
;;   :node      judgement — the M-zaif-harness-v1 phase->node table row this
;;              turn's deposit lands on, or :none if it lands on no row.
;;              PROPOSED, not found: a node here is a hypothesis the receipt
;;              either cashes or fails to cash.
;;   :receipts  lookup — commits / registry keys / worklist rows in which the
;;              machine demonstrably CONSUMED this turn at that node.
;;              Anti-glibness (inherited from the parent mission): a census row
;;              with an empty :receipts vector is decoration and ships as a
;;              typed absence, not as a finding.
;;   :receipt-grade  :direct    the receipt names or quotes this turn
;;                   :indirect  the work is traceable to this turn but no
;;                              artifact cites it
;;                   :none      nothing consumed it
;;
;; Node vocabulary is the parent mission's, not new: R1 R2 R3 R4 R5 R6 R9 R16 R17.

